$md .= "## Keyword retrieval\n\n`LegalKeywordSearch` and `legal:search` provide PostgreSQL simple-lexeme matching, bound parameters, language/category/quality filters, stable ID pagination, full source attribution and a five-second read-only query budget. Default quality is structured; review/all are explicit. No Uzbek/Russian stemming, transliteration, semantic ranking or legal/date applicability decision is claimed. Missing URLs stay null.\n\nAI migration 000003 created an initial concurrent structured-only GIN expression index. Full-corpus review/all queries reached the five-second bound; migration 000004 replaced it with an all-quality lexical GIN index after oversized-text preflight. Candidate IDs are selected first and source/JSON metadata loaded second in the same repeatable-read/read-only snapshot, avoiding a measured wide-row LIMIT plan failure; no embedding/vector extension or external engine. An exploratory EXPLAIN exceeded 44 seconds and only that AI query was canceled; this is not used as an ordinary-search latency baseline. Controlled same-snapshot bitmap-on/off plans are recorded separately, with unrelated primary-key index scans retained. Final measured indexed query: ".($plan['plans']['on']['execution_ms'] ?? 'unavailable').' ms; GIN-disabled comparison: '.(isset($plan['plans']['off']['execution_ms']) ? $plan['plans']['off']['execution_ms'].' ms' : 'timed out within its five-second budget').". Where both finish, returned IDs are compared exactly. Needs-review/all can be slower and may require narrower terms/filters.\n\n";
